session Numeric_Bound_Inference = TP_NTA_Reduction +
  description \<open>Numeric-fluent bound inference (threshold interval abstract interpretation), sitting in
    the reduction chain between TP_NTA_Reduction and TP_NTA_Reduction_Numeric. The interval domain is
    vendored IMP-free in Interval_Domain (HOL-IMP's Abs_Int0 option-order instance clashes with the
    Munta/FPS tower, so HOL-IMP itself cannot be imported here). It COMPUTES a per-fluent box
    (possibly with infinite endpoints); the fluent-list-relative loop (ginfer_thr_on /
    infer_fluent_bounds_on) needs no enum instance on the fluent type and is the interface the
    numeric reduction consumes. The executable pipeline rejects any problem whose box has an
    infinite endpoint ("bound-inference failed") since the reduction's fluent_lo/hi are finite int.
    Code ships inside the unified Converter export (no separate export here).\<close>
  theories
    Interval_Domain
    Numeric_Bound_Inference
    Numeric_Bound_Inference_Threshold
    Numeric_Bound_Inference_Guards
    Numeric_Bound_Inference_Extract
